# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE CONTRACT IN THIS REPOSITORY
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Measured during the release-branch reproduction: a fresh clone on a client
# with `core.autocrlf=true` checked `shared/src/conflict/observation.ts` out at
# 33,015 B while the stored blob is 32,380 B — 635 lines, one added CR each.
# Every BYTE-IDENTITY guard then failed on a correct commit:
#
#     sha256 of the landed module equals the sha256 of the package contract
#       expected 8cba6ef0…   received c2c955a0…
#
# Those guards are load-bearing here. Main delivers contracts that must land
# byte-for-byte, and the proof is a sha256 of the file on disk. A checkout that
# silently rewrites bytes makes that proof platform-dependent — it passed on
# the authoring workstation and on Linux, and failed on a Windows clone, for a
# commit that was in every respect correct.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree form so every checkout, on every platform,
# reproduces the stored bytes. It changes no blob: the objects are already LF.
#
# This is a normalisation, NOT an ignore. It conceals nothing and excludes no
# file from review.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be transformed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pbf binary
*.zip binary
